# Line-ending policy.
#
# Anything EXECUTED INSIDE the Linux container must be checked out with LF.
# A shell script with CRLF fails under `sh` with an unreadable
# "\r: not found", or an "unexpected end of file" when a heredoc terminator
# picks up a stray \r (setup_module1.sh in this repository is already in
# that state).
#
# The Dockerfile strips CR from scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh at build time,
# but that protection does NOT apply in development: docker-compose.yml
# bind-mounts `.:/app`, which replaces the image's processed copy with the
# HOST file. In dev the checked-out line endings are what actually run.
# This file is therefore the only durable fix.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
alembic.ini     text eol=lf

# Normalising these on checkout is safe and keeps diffs meaningful.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
